The attached image, Figure 2A and 2B from the study, presents the physical characterization of Nano-11 nanoparticles. Figure 2A, a Transmission Electron Microscopy (TEM) image, shows spherical nanoparticles with an irregular, cauliflower-like surface, primarily appearing as single particles with minimal aggregation. The scale bar indicates 50 nm. Figure 2B, representing the diameter determined by dynamic light scattering, illustrates a relatively uniform particle size distribution, with a peak between 70-80 nm, ranging broadly from 30 to 110 nm. These characteristics are central to understanding Nano-11's efficiency as a vaccine adjuvant due to its optimal size for uptake by dendritic cells and its dendrimer-like structure.